{"deliverables":["/workspace/out/q3_shareholder_letter.md","/workspace/out/earnings_call_qa_prep.md","/workspace/out/kpi_table.md"],"notes_for_reviewers":"**1. DECISION NEEDED FROM MARK, DANA AND K. BRANDT — covenant/going-concern disclosure.** Mark's 14 Oct note replaces item 3 of Priya's brief and asks us to drop the GC-approved liquidity paragraph from the letter, leave the credit agreement/waiver/Note 2 out, and let quarter-end cash stand as the whole liquidity discussion; on the call he wants "comfortable with our liquidity / strong relationship with the bank group." I did not draft it that way. The data room shows non-compliance with BOTH financial covenants at 30 Sep (4.22x vs 3.75x max; 2.64x vs 3.00x min), the waiver/amendment unexecuted, and Hartwell Pryce's draft Note 2 raising substantial doubt about going concern with $1,176.4M potentially accelerable. Citing only "$96.4M of cash" as our liquidity position, or answering "are you compliant?" with a comfort statement, would be materially misleading by omission (Rule 10b-5) — especially when 4 of the 18 submitted questions (Q04, Q10, Q14, Q16) already assume the breach. So: the letter keeps the K. Brandt-approved paragraph verbatim in the Outlook; Q04/Q05/Q10/Q13/Q14/Q16 answers stay on that language, then land on backlog/Keystone as Mark wants; no ratios are volunteered anywhere (the certificate is privileged). If the amendment is executed before the 5 Nov release, Mark and the GC can revisit the wording — but the release must reflect facts as of the release date, not hopes for 14 Nov. I also messaged Priya on this; she was not monitoring the queue.

**2. Numbers Mark's office must supply.** No tariff data exists anywhere in the data room, so Q11 (Novak) and Q17 (Becker) are explicitly marked placeholders — I will not invent tariff quantifications. The KPI reconciliation needs Finance to supply D&A and the tax effect of the excluded items; the residual bridging net income to adjusted EBITDA is $15.4M in Q3 FY2026 but only $2.5M in Q3 FY2025, which suggests prior-year adjusted EBITDA may include other addbacks. Q02's margin bridge needs Finance to confirm whether the recall charge sits in COGS or a separate line.

